From 5a553ae31b39809c181cce820ca522bbe50db468 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:26:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(blur): honor backdrop blur regions requested by clients

Applications such as GTK4 terminals ask the compositor to blur the part of
their own surface that shows the desktop, through ext_background_effect_v1,
and fall back to a window rule when the protocol is missing. Advertise the
global with the blur capability and blur exactly the requested area.

The manager keeps one double-buffered region per surface in the surface's
synced state, so set_blur_region composes with wl_surface.commit. Blur owners
read the committed region where they already own a blur node: toplevels,
popups and layer surfaces. The region is a node clip rather than a smaller
blur node, because the transparency mask stretches the surface buffer over
the whole node box and shrinking it would misalign the mask. A request turns
the blur on for that surface and an empty region turns it off; a window rule
still applies when there is no request, and a requesting view keeps its fade
and overview alpha instead of the rule's blur fade.

appearance.blur.client_requests (default true) keeps the capability
advertised while ignoring requests, and appearance.blur.enabled still wins
over both.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
